{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And you shall keep My statutes.</b> These that I have said to you — these are forbidden:" "<b>And My ordinances.</b> That you shall carry out the judgment that I command concerning one who transgresses any one of them. The sense of \"and you shall not do any of these abominations\" a second time is to include the stranger, for this commandment applies equally to the native and to the stranger, because he dwells in the land of Israel. And if you have a heart, you can understand that in the days of Jacob, who took two sisters in Haran, and after him Amram, who took his aunt in Egypt — they were not defiled by them:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:46.591954016Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}